## Why This Is Asked
Tests designing scalable, low-latency timing primitives under heavy load and NUMA constraints; checks concurrency, memory locality, and wakeup efficiency for high-performance services.

## Key Concepts
- Timer data structures: hierarchical timer wheel with per-core buckets and a global wheel
- NUMA-aware placement and cross-socket wakeups
- Concurrency: fine-grained locking or lock-free structures, generation IDs, and cancel semantics
- Tickless vs periodic: clock sources and tick alignment
- Testing: microbenchmarks, drift under load, and cross-core wakeups

